      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ca12dc14-1b71-5336-937d-72bc37e8aa13",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Rolls-Royce Welland, Derwent, Proteus, Olympus, Pegasus\n- People: Stanley Hooker\n- Companies: Rolls-Royce, Bristol Aero Engines\n- Places: River Welland, east of England\n- Concepts: Jet engine naming, continuous flow\n\nFacts:\n- The River Welland is a lowland river in the east of England that is about 65 miles long.\n- Stanley Hooker lived from 30 September 1907 to 24 May 1984.\n- Stanley Hooker was a mathematician and jet engine engineer who worked first at Rolls-Royce on early engine designs such as the Welland and Derwent.\n- Stanley Hooker later worked at Bristol Aero Engines, where he helped bring the Proteus turboprop and Olympus turbojet to market and designed the Pegasus vectored-thrust turbofan used in the Hawker Siddeley Harrier.\n- The Rolls-Royce Welland was named after the River Welland.\n- Rolls-Royce named its early jet engines after rivers to reflect the idea of continuous flow, with air flowing through an engine and water flowing in a river.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b1b609e5-fe2a-5f4f-8c5a-eeeacb147483",
        "text": "Page: Rolls-Royce Welland. Sentence: The name Welland is taken from the River Welland, in keeping with the Rolls-Royce policy of naming early jet engines after rivers based on the idea of continuous flow, air through the engine and water in a river.\nPage: River Welland. Sentence: The River Welland is a lowland river in the east of England, some 65 mi long.\nPage: Stanley Hooker. Sentence: Sir Stanley George Hooker, FRS, DPhil, BSc, FRAeS, MIMechE, FAAAS, (30 September 1907 – 24 May 1984) was a Mathematician and jet engine engineer, first at Rolls-Royce where he worked on the earliest designs such as the Welland and Derwent, and later at Bristol Aero Engines where he helped bring the troubled Proteus turboprop, and Olympus turbojet to market, and then designed the famous Pegasus vectored thrust turbofan used in the Hawker Siddeley Harrier.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
